# The catalog and the prepared preview images are binary. Marking them so
# stops git attempting a textual diff, attempting a merge it cannot do, or
# rewriting line endings inside them on a different platform.
#
# This matters more than it looks. data/modbench.db is checked in (see
# README, "Running it"), and two people changing it on the same branch
# produces a conflict git cannot resolve -- the only outcomes are "keep
# mine" or "keep theirs", wholesale. There is no merging two people's part
# approvals. The workflow in README "Working with someone else" exists to
# keep that from happening; this line makes sure git fails loudly rather
# than quietly producing a corrupt database if it ever does.
data/modbench.db binary
*.webp binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary

# Generated. Collapsed in diffs and PR reviews so a catalog re-run does
# not bury a real change under thousands of lines.
pnpm-lock.yaml -diff linguist-generated
data/fixtures/shape-fallbacks.json -diff
data/fixtures/asset-states.json -diff
data/fixtures/phash-raw-results.json -diff
data/fixtures/dedup-phash-normalised.json -diff
